------------------------------------------------------------
Personal Note
------------------------------------------------------------

Today was an important conceptual milestone.

The most valuable result was not adding another class,
but understanding ownership and object state.

Objects are no longer viewed as collections of procedures.

Instead, they are long-lived entities that own knowledge,
coordinate responsibilities, and collaborate with other objects.

This marks the transition from procedural programming
to a genuinely object-oriented architecture.